module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Properties.GabberResult.Colimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionsAndBounds.FiniteTypeSubobjects

/-!
# Tag 01PG, the colimit assertion, from the affine sections statement alone

[Stacks, Tag 01PG] says that on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme a quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module is the **directed colimit of its quasi-coherent submodules of finite type**. The
assertion has two halves, which are separately statable:

* *directedness*: the category of those submodules is filtered. Proved, unconditionally on the
  scheme, as `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_isFiltered`
  (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ResolutionsAndBounds/FiniteTypeSubobjects.lean`), and registered
  against the tag by `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineSubsheaf/Directedness.lean`.
* *the colimit*: the canonical cocone out of that category, with vertex `F`, is colimiting. Until
  this file **no `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsColimit` statement about
  `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone` existed in either tree** — the
  definition and one docstring were its only two occurrences.

This file states the colimit assertion and proves it from **one** input, the affine sections
statement: every section of `F` over an affine open of `X` is a section of some finite type
quasi-coherent submodule of `F` *on the whole of `X`*. That is where quasi-compactness and
quasi-separatedness genuinely enter, and it is [Stacks, Tag 01PF]; it is not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `AffineSections`: the affine sections statement, as a named proposition.

## Main results

* `isColimit_of_affineSections`: **the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01PG] from the affine
  sections statement alone**, and `nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections` in the `Nonempty` form.
* `hasColimitsOfShape_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject`: the diagram has a colimit at all, which
  the statement above needs in order to speak of the comparison map.

## Implementation notes

The argument is the last sentence of the source's proof and is purely formal once the two inputs
are available. It is **the proof of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration.isColimit_cocone_of_exists_mem`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Properties/GabberResult/Colimit.lean`) with one predicate
changed**: that theorem is the same assertion for the subobjects generated by at most `κ` local
sections — [Stacks, Tag 077N] — over the same `F : X.Modules`, with a `Subobject`-indexed diagram
and canonical cocone built identically, and the predicate is used nowhere in its proof. Every
helper it needs is `public`, so nothing is copied here but the five-line skeleton:

* the comparison map out of the colimit is a **monomorphism**, because the index category is
  filtered and filtered colimits in `X.Modules` are exact, so `colim` preserves the monomorphism
  of diagrams whose components are the inclusions of the subobjects;
* it is **locally surjective** on sections, because the affine opens are a basis and the affine
  sections hypothesis holds on them;
* a monomorphism of `𝒪_X`-modules which is locally surjective on sections is an isomorphism
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration.isIso_of_mono_of_locallySurjective`), and a cocone
  whose comparison map is an isomorphism is colimiting.

Two set-up points, both inherited from that file and both load-bearing. The index category is the
full subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Subobject F` cut out by the property, so it lives in
`Type (u + 1)` while `AB5OfSize.{u, u}` speaks about shapes in `Type u`; exactness is therefore
transported from the small model, which exists because `X.Modules` is well-powered. And
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cocone.isColimitOfIsIsoColimMapι` is about `colimMap` of the cocone's
natural transformation rather than about `colimit.desc`, so
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration.colimMap_comp_constPointIso` identifies the two; that
isomorphism is written out rather than named, because naming it with `set` hides it from instance
search.

Note which hypotheses are **not** used: neither `CompactSpace X` nor `QuasiSeparatedSpace X`
appears below. The reduction is unconditional on the scheme, exactly as the corresponding
reduction for algebra sheaves is
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`);
the two hypotheses of the tag are consumed entirely by `AffineSections`.

## What this does not do, and no stacks attribute

**No stacks attribute for the `colimit` label of 01PG is attached, and none may be.**
`AffineSections F` is a
hypothesis the tag does not grant, so the covering set of that label is not complete. It is the
single remaining input, and its route is [Stacks, Tag 01PF] — for `U` an affine open of `X` and
`s` a section of `F` over `U`, the subsheaf of `F|_U` generated by `s` is quasi-coherent of finite
type, and 01PF extends it to a finite type quasi-coherent submodule of `F` on all of `X`. The two
ends of 01PF's affine induction are proved
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffineSubsheaf.exists_isFiniteType_submodule_eq_top_on` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_quasicoherentSubobject_restrict`, the latter carrying the 01PE
attribute), its glueing step is proved
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SubmoduleGlueOpens/Basic.lean` with
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SubmoduleGlueLocality/Basic.lean`), and what the induction still
lacks is recorded in the latter file's module documentation.

This is **not** [Stacks, Tag 01PK], which is about finitely *presented* modules that need not be
submodules and whose proof uses 01PJ, 0032 and 009E.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077N)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PGColimit

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The diagram of finite type quasi-coherent subobjects of `F` is essentially small: its objects
form a `Type (u + 1)`, but `X.Modules` is well-powered, so `F` has only `u`-many subobjects up to
isomorphism. -/
instance essentiallySmall_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject (F : X.Modules) :
    EssentiallySmall.{u} (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) :=
  inferInstance

/-- The diagram of finite type quasi-coherent subobjects of `F` has a colimit in `X.Modules`. -/
theorem hasColimitsOfShape_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject (F : X.Modules) :
    HasColimitsOfShape (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) X.Modules :=
  hasColimitsOfShape_of_essentiallySmall _ _

/-- **The affine sections statement.** Every section of `F` over an affine open of `X` is a
section of some finite type quasi-coherent submodule of `F` on the whole of `X`.

This is the single input of `isColimit_of_affineSections`, and it is where the quasi-compactness
and quasi-separatedness of [Stacks, Tag 01PG] enter: the submodule it asks for is global while the
section is given only over one affine open. Its route is [Stacks, Tag 01PF]. -/
def AffineSections (F : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (s : Γ(F, U.1)),
    ∃ G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F, s ∈ Set.range (G.obj.arrow.app U.1)

/-- **The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01PG], from the affine sections statement alone.** A
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module is the colimit of its finite type quasi-coherent submodules, with the
canonical inclusions as the legs, as soon as every section over an affine open is a section of one
of them.

No hypothesis on `X` is used: the filteredness of the index category is proved unconditionally,
and the affine sections hypothesis absorbs the quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the
tag. **No attribute is attached**: `hgen` is a hypothesis the tag does not have. -/
def isColimit_of_affineSections (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hgen : AffineSections F) :
    IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F) := by
  classical
  have hcol : HasColimitsOfShape (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) X.Modules :=
    hasColimitsOfShape_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F
  have : IsFiltered (SmallModel (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F)) :=
    IsFiltered.of_equivalence (equivSmallModel _)
  have : HasExactColimitsOfShape (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) X.Modules :=
    HasExactColimitsOfShape.of_domain_equivalence X.Modules (equivSmallModel _).symm
  have : IsConnected (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) := IsFiltered.isConnected _
  have : ∀ G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F,
      Mono ((finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F).ι.app G) :=
    fun G => Subobject.arrow_mono G.obj
  have : Mono (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F).ι := NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app _
  have hmcm : Mono (colimMap (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F).ι) := by
    rw [colimMap_eq]
    exact Functor.map_mono _ _
  have hfac := colimMap_comp_constPointIso (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F)
  have hmc : Mono (colimit.desc (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F)
      (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F)) :=
    mono_of_comp_iso_eq _ hfac hmcm
  have hloc : ∀ (U : X.Opens) (s : Γ(F, U)) (x : X), x ∈ U →
      ∃ V : X.Opens, ∃ hVU : V ≤ U, x ∈ V ∧
        F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op s ∈
          Set.range ((colimit.desc (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F)
            (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F)).app V) := by
    intro U s x hxU
    obtain ⟨-, ⟨V, hVaff, rfl⟩, hxV, hVU⟩ :=
      X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (show x ∈ (U : Set X) from hxU) U.isOpen
    have hle : V ≤ U := hVU
    obtain ⟨G, y, hy⟩ := hgen ⟨V, hVaff⟩ (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op s)
    have hcomp : colimit.ι (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F) G ≫
        colimit.desc (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F)
          (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F) = G.obj.arrow :=
      colimit.ι_desc _ _
    exact ⟨V, hle, hxV, ⟨(colimit.ι (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F) G).app V y,
      (comp_app_apply _ _ V y).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (fun f : (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F).obj G ⟶ F => f.app V y)
          hcomp).trans hy)⟩⟩
  have hiso : IsIso (colimit.desc (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectFunctor F)
      (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F)) :=
    @isIso_of_mono_of_locallySurjective X _ _ _ hmc hloc
  have : IsIso (colimMap (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F).ι) :=
    isIso_of_comp_iso_eq _ hfac hiso
  exact Cocone.isColimitOfIsIsoColimMapι _

/-- `isColimit_of_affineSections` in the `Nonempty` form, which is how the colimit assertion of a
tag is usually stated. -/
theorem nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hgen : AffineSections F) :
    Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F)) :=
  ⟨isColimit_of_affineSections F hgen⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PGColimit

end
